                <div class="section_11">
                    <h2 class="main_heading">
                        The four temperaments
                    </h2>
                    <p class="description">
                        We'll delve into how your personality profile aligns with the four
                        temperaments types. These temperaments serve to encapsulate
                        fundamental patterns in human cognition and behavior. They
                        offer a broader lens for categorizing individuals beyond
                        personality types, aiding in swiftly grasping the driving
                        forces behind people's actions. Each temperament delineates
                        a distinct method of engaging with the world.
                    </p>
                    <p class="description" style="margin: 10px;">
                        <b>The Guardians, </b>one of the four temperaments, are known for their commitment to
                        stability, order, and tradition. They value security, reliability,
                        and adherence to established norms. Guardians are dependable
                        individuals who prioritize duty, responsibility, and practicality
                        in their approach to life. They often excel in roles that require
                        organization, consistency, and attention to detail. Guardians
                        strive to uphold societal structures and maintain a sense of
                        continuity, making them pillars of support and stability within
                        their communities.
                    </p>
                    <p class="description" style="margin: 10px;">
                        <b>The Artisans,</b>one of the four temperaments, are characterized by their spontaneity,
                        adaptability, and focus on the present moment. They thrive on excitement, variety, and
                        hands-on experiences. Artisans are known for their resourcefulness, creativity, and
                        ability to think on their feet. They embrace challenges and enjoy exploring new
                        opportunities without being bound by rigid structures or conventions. Artisans excel
                        in roles that require flexibility, quick thinking, and the ability to troubleshoot in
                        dynamic environments. They bring energy, innovation, and a zest for life to whatever they
                        pursue.
                    </p>
                    <p class="description" style="margin: 10px;">
                        <b>The Rationals,</b>one of the four temperaments, are marked by their analytical prowess,
                        strategic thinking, and quest for knowledge. They are driven by a desire to understand
                        complex systems and uncover underlying principles governing the world around them.
                        Rationals excel in problem-solving, critical analysis, and long-term planning. They are
                        known for their logical reasoning, innovative ideas, and willingness to challenge
                        conventional wisdom. Rationals are drawn to fields that require deep intellectual
                        engagement, such as science, technology, engineering, and philosophy.
                        They are visionaries who seek to shape the future through their insights and discoveries.
                    </p>
                    <p class="description" style="margin: 10px;">
                        <b>The Idealists,</b>one of the four temperaments, are characterized by their compassion,
                        empathy, and commitment to personal values. They are driven by a desire to create positive
                        change in the world and to foster deeper connections with others. Idealists are known for
                        their optimism, idealism, and belief in the inherent goodness of humanity. They strive
                        for authenticity, authenticity, and integrity in all aspects of their lives.
                        Idealists often pursue careers in helping professions, such as counseling, teaching,
                        social work, and advocacy. They are passionate about social justice, creativity,
                        and the pursuit of meaningful relationships. Idealists seek to inspire others and
                        to make a difference in the world through their actions and beliefs.
                    </p>
                    <p class="description">
                        Your scores reflect how closely your personality aligns with each of the four temperament types.
                        Typically, your highest score indicates the temperament type that resonates most with your
                        personality. However, if you have similar scores across multiple temperament types, you may
                        adapt your style based on the circumstances.

                    </p>

