                        solutions in both professional and personal settings. Your ability to communicate clearly and
                        assertively helps you navigate complex situations and build strong relationships with colleagues
                        and clients.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Hands-On Approach to Learning:</b> ESTPs have a hands-on approach to
                        learning and problem-solving. You prefer to learn by doing, actively engaging with tasks and
                        projects to gain practical experience and insights. You thrive in environments that allow you to
                        apply your skills in real-world scenarios and explore new opportunities for growth and
                        development.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Adaptable and Flexible:</b> ESTPs are highly adaptable and flexible
                        individuals who thrive in dynamic work environments. You enjoy taking on new challenges and
                        exploring different avenues for success. Your ability to adapt to changing circumstances and
                        embrace uncertainty allows you to thrive in roles that require quick thinking and on-the-spot
                        decision-making.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Ability to Think Under Pressure:</b> ESTPs excel in high-pressure
                        situations where they can think quickly and make decisive decisions. Your ability to stay calm
                        and composed under pressure instills confidence in your colleagues and enables you to
                        effectively manage crises and navigate challenging situations with ease.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Preference for Action Over Planning:</b> While you value strategic
                        thinking, ESTPs are more inclined to prioritize action over detailed planning. You prefer to
                        dive into projects headfirst, trusting your instincts and practical skills to guide you along
                        the way. Your willingness to take risks and embrace uncertainty often leads to innovative
                        solutions and breakthroughs in your work.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="description">In summary, your personality at work as an ESTP is characterized by your
                    action-oriented problem-solving, natural leadership abilities, strong negotiation skills, hands-on
                    approach to learning, adaptability, ability to think under pressure, and preference for action over
                    planning. These traits make you well-suited for roles that require quick decision-making, effective
                    communication, and the ability to thrive in dynamic and challenging environments.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                 </div>
                 <br />
                <p class="description top-extra-space">Your leadership style:</p> 
                                <p class="description">
                    As an ESTP, your leadership style is characterized by your dynamic and action-oriented approach,
                    your ability to think on your feet, and your natural charisma. Here's an overview of your leadership
                    style:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Energetic and Charismatic:</b> ESTP leaders are known for their high
                        energy levels, enthusiasm, and charismatic presence. You have a natural ability to inspire and
                        motivate others, drawing people in with your dynamic personality and engaging communication
                        style. Your charisma enables you to build strong relationships with your team members and
                        stakeholders, fostering a positive and supportive work environment.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Action-Oriented and Decisive:</b> You thrive in fast-paced environments
                        where you can take decisive action and drive results. ESTP leaders are highly action-oriented,
                        preferring to dive into projects headfirst and tackle challenges as they arise. Your ability to
                        think on your feet and make quick decisions in high-pressure situations allows you to navigate
                        complex problems effectively and keep projects moving forward.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Hands-On and Practical:</b> ESTP leaders prefer a hands-on and practical
                        approach to leadership. You lead by example, actively participating in projects and initiatives
                        alongside your team members. Your willingness to roll up your sleeves and get your hands dirty
                        instills confidence in your team and demonstrates your commitment to achieving shared goals. You
                        excel in situations that require practical problem-solving skills and a focus on tangible
                        results.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Flexible and Adaptable:</b> You thrive in environments that offer variety,
                        challenge, and opportunities for growth. ESTP leaders are highly adaptable, able to pivot
                        quickly in response to changing circumstances and navigate uncertainty with confidence. Your
                        flexibility enables you to remain agile in dynamic environments, adjusting your approach as
                        needed to achieve optimal outcomes.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Risk-Taker and Innovator:</b> You are comfortable taking risks and
                        exploring new ideas and opportunities. ESTP leaders are natural innovators, always on the
                        lookout for ways to improve processes, drive innovation, and capitalize on emerging trends. Your
                        willingness to embrace change and push boundaries inspires creativity and innovation within your
                        team, driving continuous improvement and growth.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Effective Communicator and Influencer:</b> You excel in communication and
                        are skilled at persuading and influencing others to buy into your vision and ideas. ESTP leaders
                        are adept at articulating their thoughts and rallying support for their initiatives, using their
                        persuasive abilities to inspire action and drive positive change. Your ability to build rapport
                        and connect with diverse audiences makes you an effective communicator and influencer.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="description">In summary, your leadership style as an ESTP is characterized by your energy,
                    charisma, action-oriented approach, and ability to adapt to change. You thrive in fast-paced
                    environments, where you can take decisive action, drive innovation, and inspire others to achieve
                    their full potential. Your hands-on leadership style and natural charisma make you a dynamic and
                    influential leader in any organization.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                 <br/>
                <p class="description top-extra-space">Your teamwork style:</p>
                <p class="description">
                    As an ESTP, your teamwork style is characterized by your energetic and action-oriented approach,
                    your ability to adapt quickly to changing situations, your knack for thinking on your feet, your
                    focus on tangible results, and your talent for building rapport with diverse team members. Here's an
                    overview of your teamwork style:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Energetic and Action-Oriented Approach: </b>ESTPs are known for their high
                        energy levels and their preference for taking action. In team settings, you are often the one to
                        jump into tasks enthusiastically and lead by example. Your dynamic energy motivates team members
                        and drives progress on projects and initiatives.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Adaptability: </b> ESTPs excel in adapting to new situations and
                        environments. You thrive in dynamic team settings where change is constant, quickly adjusting
                        your approach to meet evolving challenges. Your adaptability makes you a valuable asset in teams
                        facing uncertainty, as you can easily pivot and find solutions on the fly.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Quick Thinking and Problem-Solving Skills: </b>ESTPs have a natural talent
                        for thinking on their feet and finding practical solutions to problems. In team settings, you
                        are adept at identifying issues and implementing solutions in real time. Your ability to remain
                        calm and composed under pressure allows you to tackle challenges with confidence and efficiency.
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Focus on Tangible Results: </b> ESTPs are results-oriented individuals who
                        prefer to focus on concrete outcomes. In team projects, you prioritize tasks that contribute
                        directly to achieving goals and objectives. Your drive to see tangible results motivates team
                        members and helps keep projects on track toward successful completion.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Talent for Building Rapport: </b> ESTPs possess excellent interpersonal
                        skills and have a knack for building rapport with people from diverse backgrounds. You enjoy
                        collaborating with team members and thrive in environments where teamwork and camaraderie are
                        valued. Your ability to connect with others fosters a positive team dynamic and encourages
                        collaboration and open communication.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="description">In summary, your teamwork style as an ESTP is characterized by your energetic and
                    action-oriented approach, adaptability, quick thinking and problem-solving skills, focus on tangible
                    results, and talent for building rapport with diverse team members. You bring enthusiasm,
                    flexibility, and a results-driven mindset to team collaborations, driving progress and fostering
                    positive relationships within the group.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p class="description top-extra-space">For a better you:</p>
                <p class="description">As an ESTP, here are some areas you might consider for improvement:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Long-Term Planning:</b> ESTPs often enjoy living in the moment and may
                        struggle with long-term planning and goal setting. Practice setting clear, achievable long-term
                        goals and breaking them down into smaller, actionable steps to help you stay focused and
                        motivated over time.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Consideration of Consequences:</b> ESTPs can be spontaneous and
                        risk-taking, sometimes without fully considering the potential consequences of their actions.
                        Practice taking a moment to evaluate potential outcomes before making decisions, especially in
                        important or high-stakes situations.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Active Listening:</b> ESTPs may have a tendency to dominate conversations
                        and focus more on expressing their own ideas rather than listening to others. Practice active
                        listening techniques, such as summarizing and reflecting back what others have said, to
                        demonstrate empathy and understanding in your interactions.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Emotional Awareness:</b> ESTPs may struggle with recognizing and
                        expressing their own emotions, as well as understanding the emotions of others. Practice
                        developing your emotional awareness and empathy by actively tuning into your own feelings and
                        considering the perspectives and emotions of those around you.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Attention to Detail:</b> ESTPs may overlook details in their eagerness to
                        take action and experience new things. Practice paying attention to details and taking the time
                        to ensure accuracy and thoroughness in your work and relationships.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Conflict Resolution:</b> ESTPs may prefer to avoid conflict or may become
                        impatient with interpersonal disagreements. Practice developing your conflict resolution skills
                        by remaining calm, listening actively, and seeking mutually beneficial solutions when conflicts
                        arise.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Follow-Through:</b> ESTPs may have many ideas and projects in mind but may
                        struggle with follow-through and completing tasks. Practice setting priorities, staying
                        organized, and maintaining focus to see projects through to completion.</li>
                    <li class="list-item"><b> Self-Reflection:</b> ESTPs may benefit from taking time to reflect on
                        their experiences, decisions, and interactions with others. Practice journaling, meditation, or
                        other self-reflection techniques to help you gain insight into yourself and your actions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="description">By focusing on these areas for improvement, you can continue to develop and grow
                    as an ESTP, leveraging your strengths while addressing potential challenges in your personal and
                    professional life.</p>
            </div>
